# PVC Runtime Rules (English Canonical)

> Korean siblings: `runtime/platform-targets.mdc`, `dependency-policy.mdc`, `build-output.mdc`.

## 1. Platform Targets

- Supported runtimes/browsers/OS come from **`project-context`**—do not invent bleeding-edge APIs.
- Align local/CI/prod major versions (Twelve-Factor parity).
- Polyfill/transpile only when required by declared targets; respect `browserslist` / `tsconfig.target`.
- Avoid hardcoded absolute OS paths; document native addon platform limits.

## 2. Dependency Policy

- Add a package only if clear win vs hand-roll, acceptable license/size/maintenance, no duplicate, and approval when large.
- No unapproved mass upgrades or framework swaps.
- Commit lockfiles; run ecosystem audit tools; don’t ignore Critical/High without recorded risk acceptance.
- Watch typosquatting and risky install scripts; remove unused deps after reference checks.

## 3. Build Output

- Don’t commit build artifacts as source of truth.
- Production builds: minify, tree-shake, dead-code eliminate.
- Budgets from `project-context` + Web Vitals; exceed → measure → report → optimize or get approval.
- Prefer named/path imports over whole-library imports; hash static assets; don’t ship huge raw media.
